# Frontend build-time configuration. Copy this file to .env.local (or set the same
# variable in your host's build settings) and fill it in. Never commit .env files.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* values when the app is BUILT, not when it runs: change the
# value, then rebuild. It is read in src/main.jsx and checked by the build itself
# (vite.config.js) against the rules in src/config/apiBaseUrl.js.

# Origin of the ShopStock API: scheme://host[:port]. Requests are sent to
# `${VITE_API_BASE_URL}/api/...`. No path, query string or credentials; a trailing
# slash is accepted and removed.
#
#   PRODUCTION build (`npm run build`, what the host runs): REQUIRED. It must be the
#   backend's HTTPS origin, for example https://api.example.com. The build FAILS if it
#   is missing, malformed, http://, carries a path, or points at localhost or any
#   loopback address, so a production bundle can never silently target the wrong host.
#
#   PREVIEW build (`npm run build:preview`): the explicit way to build against a local
#   or http backend, for example http://localhost:4000. Leave it unset to use the same
#   origin. Do not deploy a preview build.
#
#   DEVELOPMENT (`npm run dev`): optional; unset means the same origin. There is no dev
#   proxy, so for a local backend set http://localhost:4000 (for example in .env.local)
#   and make sure the backend's CORS_ORIGIN (backend/.env.example) lists the origin the
#   app is served from, for example http://localhost:5173.
#
# Per-mode overrides that must not be committed go in .env.production.local or
# .env.preview.local.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
